{{also|scheissen|schéissen}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|de|scheissen}} {{qualifier|Switzerland|Liechtenstein}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|schīzen}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*skītaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*skeyd-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*sḱeyd-||to part with, separate, cut off}}. Compare Low German {{m|nds|schieten}}, Dutch {{m|nl|schijten}}, and English (verb) ''[[shit]]'', Danish {{m|da|skide}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃaɪ̯sn̩/|/ˈʃaɪ̯sən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-scheißen.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=1|scheißt|schiss|geschissen|past subjunctive=schisse}}

# {{lb|de|vulgar}} to [[shit]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''scheiß'''' mir gleich in die Hose!|t=I'm about to '''shit''' my pants!}}

====Conjugation====
Before 1996, the past tense form was {{m|de|schiß}}, but, per the 1996 German Spelling Reform, the correct spelling is now {{m|de|schiss}}.
{{de-conj-strong|scheiß|schiss|geschissen|h||||a|a|||a}}

